# Modeling Report: A-mcm-2023-c

## Problem Framing

The case is **MCM 2023 Problem C, “Predicting Wordle Results.”** Wordle asks a player to identify a valid five-letter English word in at most six guesses. Each guess produces position-wise feedback: green (correct letter and position), yellow (correct letter, wrong position), or unmarked/gray (letter not usable in that position or word).

The modeling objective is to predict Wordle outcomes from the supplied 2023 historical dataset. The summary does not expose the full subquestion text or complete column semantics, so target definitions and feature availability must be confirmed during authorized data parsing; unresolved requirements remain **pending**.

